      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do the panels attach to my bed?",
            "answer": "<p>No. They fix to the wall on aluminium brackets, so they work with any bed, including divans and bed frames.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What’s in each box?",
            "answer": "<p>4 panels, the aluminium mounting brackets and screws, plus step-by-step instructions.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it work on my wall?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. Our patented screws grip plasterboard firmly, with no wall plugs needed. For brick, block or concrete walls, simply pre-drill 5mm holes first. Each screw holds up to 22kg.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Where should the bottom row start?",
            "answer": "<p>Usually just below the top of your mattress, or from the skirting board for a full feature wall.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What about plug sockets and light switches?",
            "answer": "<p>You can cut an opening in a panel so the socket or switch stays accessible. Mark the position on the back of the panel, cut through the wooden base with a jigsaw, then trim the foam and fabric neatly with a sharp craft knife. Or, if you’d rather not cut, use a flat plug extension lead to bring power to the side of your headboard. Never cover a socket or switch completely with a panel. If you’d like a socket moved, please use a qualified electrician.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I clean them?",
            "answer": "<p>Vintage leather and metallic: wipe with a damp cloth. Velvet, micro suede, weave and bouclé: vacuum with a soft brush and spot-clean gently.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Are the fabrics fire-tested?",
            "answer": "<p>Fire safety information is available on request. Please contact our team.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
